# Goal 9: Export bridge test functions (double)

## Functions
`bridge___tan`, `bridge___sin_pi`, `bridge___rem_pio2_internal`, `bridge___ctans`

## C Source
- __tan: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/trigd.c
- __sin_pi: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/gammad.c (or trigd.c)
- __rem_pio2_internal: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/internal/trigd.c
- __ctans: /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexd/internal/ctrigd.c

## Rust Source
/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s2/src/ — internal functions exist but
bridge wrappers for testing are not exported

## Problem
The test harness uses `bridge_` prefixed wrapper functions to test internal
functions that have complex signatures. These bridge functions are not
implemented in the Rust binary.

Expected test outputs:
```
bridge___rem_pio2_internal([0x1.4p+2], e0=0, nx=1) = 3 y=[0x1.268380ccde2ddp-2, -0x1.3c9ca64f45053p-56]
bridge___rem_pio2_internal([0x1p+0], e0=2, nx=1) = 3 y=[-0x1.6cbe3f9990e92p-1, 0x1.61b1acd85d7d7p-55]
bridge___tan 0x1p-1 0x0p+0 1 = 0x1.17b4f5bf3474ap-1
bridge___tan 0x1p-1 0x0p+0 -1 = -0x1.d49ad7e47c0a3p+0
bridge___tan 0x0p+0 0x0p+0 1 = 0x0p+0
bridge___tan 0x1.921fb54442d18p-1 0x0p+0 1 = 0x1.fffffffffffffp-1
bridge___sin_pi 0x1p-1 = 0x1p+0
bridge___sin_pi 0x1p+0 = -0x0p+0
bridge___sin_pi 0x1p-2 = 0x1.6a09e667f3bccp-1
bridge___sin_pi -0x1p-1 = -0x1p+0
bridge___ctans(0x1p+0+0x1p+0i) = 0x1.ac4b543086b7bp+1
bridge___ctans(0x0p+0+0x1p-1i) = 0x1.160eaa3b3ea9fp-1
```

## What Needs to Change
Add `#[no_mangle] pub extern "C"` bridge wrapper functions in lib.rs that call
the corresponding internal Rust functions with the appropriate signatures.

## Success Criteria
- All 12 test cases above produce bitwise-exact output matching C
